<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-12367] Disable by default bash pipefail/errexit/nounset options from startup scripts</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-12367</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>

&lt;p&gt;A fix for &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-11216&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-11216&lt;/a&gt; introduced following bash options&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;set -o nounset
set -o errexit
set -o pipefail
set -o errtrace
set -o functrace
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;to Ignite startup scripts. These options cause scripts to fail immediately&lt;br/&gt;
1. on any error&lt;br/&gt;
2. on any error in child process&lt;br/&gt;
3. on any undeclared variable&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, some, if not all non-zero errorcodes are valid and should not cause scripts to fail.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Due to huge number of ignite startup scripts and possible configurations, risk is very high that all possible problems were not found and more to go with similar symptoms: scripts just silently exit at random.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
